        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Top medical groups band together to ease confusion from Trump administration’s changing immunization advice</p><p>Leading US medical groups are urging people to get updated flu and Covid-19 vaccinations this fall, banding together on Wednesday to issue shot guidelines – and highlight the science behind them – saying they hope to ease confusion caused by the Trump administration’s changing advice.</p><p>Flu vaccinations are beginning and the latest coronavirus shots are starting to arrive after the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approved this year’s updated versions last week. Winter also brings another vaccine-preventable risk called RSV.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/02/flu-covid-vaccines-guidance\">Continue reading...</a>"
